      "content": "Answer the following question with a single MySQL SQL query against the current database. Explore the semantic network and verify with mysql_query as needed. The SELECT list must contain exactly the columns the question asks for, in the asked order. When the final SQL is verified, call the submit_SQL tool with it.\n\nThe following hints are provided to help you write the SQL:\n\n## Gold Tables\n- SIS_SUBJECT_CODE\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT\n- TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED\n- STUDENT_DEPARTMENT\n\n## Column Mapping\n- school name: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.SCHOOL_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME\n- department name: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME\n- average total units: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- total units range: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- total units variance: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS\n- degree-granting subjects: SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING, SIS_DEPARTMENT.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING\n- 2022 academic year: COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR\n- Mathematics department (Course 18): SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT\n- School of Engineering: SIS_DEPARTMENT.SCHOOL_NAME\n- Management: SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE\n- total student enrollment: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- most popular course: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE\n- course enrollment: TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS\n- reason: \n\n## Join Keys\n- SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE <-> SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER\n- COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE <-> SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE\n- SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n- STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE <-> TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE\n\n## Domain Knowledge\n- \"math\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_NAME = 'Mathematics'\"\n- \"degree-granting\" is predicated by \"TABLE.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'\"\n- \"Course 18\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT = '18'\"\n- \"Course 15\" is predicated by \"UPPER(TABLE.SIS_ADMIN_DEPARTMENT_NAME) = 'MANAGEMENT'\"\n- \"Management\" is predicated by \"TABLE.DEPARTMENT_CODE = '15'\"\n\n## Subquery Decomposition\n1. For each department, give the department name and calculate the average, range, and variance of the total units for subjects offered in the 2022 academic year that are degree granting, but only include departments that are not 'Mathematics' (Course 18).\n```sql\nSELECT SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units, MAX(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range, VARIANCE(COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ON SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER = SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE WHERE COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics' AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <> '18' GROUP BY SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME ORDER BY total_units_range DESC;\n```\n2. For each department, give the department name and calculate the total number of students enrolled in courses offered by that department in the School of Engineering, where the total number of enrolled students is greater than 50, and restrict the results to departments that grant degrees and exclude the Department of Management (Course 15).\n```sql\nSELECT s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SUM(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS total_enrollment FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT s JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t ON s.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t.OFFER_DEPT_CODE JOIN STUDENT_DEPARTMENT d ON t.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE s.SCHOOL_NAME = 'Engineering' AND s.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND s.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '15' GROUP BY s.DEPARTMENT_NAME HAVING SUM(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) > 50;\n```\n3. For each school, list the school name, the department name, and calculate the average, range, and variance of the total units for subjects offered in the 2022 academic year that are degree granting, but only include departments that are not 'Mathematics' (Course 18). For each school, also include a grand total for all departments in that school in the format of (school name, null, aggregated values).\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME, SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.SCHOOL_NAME, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS FROM SIS_SUBJECT_CODE JOIN SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ON SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER = SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE JOIN COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED ON SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE = COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE WHERE COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.ACADEMIC_YEAR = 2022 AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics' AND SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT <> '18' ) SELECT SCHOOL_NAME, DEPARTMENT_NAME, AVG(TOTAL_UNITS) AS avg_total_units, MAX(TOTAL_UNITS) - MIN(TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_range, VARIANCE(TOTAL_UNITS) AS total_units_variance FROM inner_cte GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME, DEPARTMENT_NAME WITH ROLLUP HAVING SCHOOL_NAME IS NOT NULL ORDER BY SCHOOL_NAME, DEPARTMENT_NAME\n```\n4. Among departments in the School of Engineering that grant degrees (excluding the Department of Management), which departments have a total student enrollment in their offered courses greater than 50, and for each such department, what is the most popular course (by enrollment) they offer and its enrollment count?\n```sql\nWITH inner_cte AS ( SELECT s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s.DEPARTMENT_CODE, SUM(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) AS total_enrollment FROM SIS_DEPARTMENT s JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t ON s.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t.OFFER_DEPT_CODE JOIN STUDENT_DEPARTMENT d ON t.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = d.DEPARTMENT_CODE WHERE s.SCHOOL_NAME = 'Engineering' AND s.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y' AND s.DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '15' GROUP BY s.DEPARTMENT_NAME, s.DEPARTMENT_CODE HAVING SUM(t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) > 50 ) SELECT ic.DEPARTMENT_NAME, ic.total_enrollment, t.SUBJECT_TITLE AS Most_Popular_Course, t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS AS Course_Enrollment FROM inner_cte ic JOIN TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t ON ic.DEPARTMENT_CODE = t.OFFER_DEPT_CODE WHERE t.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS = ( SELECT MAX(t2.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) FROM TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED t2 WHERE t2.OFFER_DEPT_CODE = ic.DEPARTMENT_CODE ) ORDER BY ic.total_enrollment DESC;\n```\n\n## Question\nFor each school and department, list the school name, department name, average total units, range of total units, and variance of total units for degree-granting subjects offered in the 2022 academic year, excluding the Mathematics department (Course 18), and include a grand total for all departments in each school (with department name as null). Also, for each department in the School of Engineering (excluding Management) that grants degrees and has a total student enrollment in its offered courses greater than 50, list the department name, total enrollment, the most popular course by enrollment, and its enrollment count. For each result, indicate the reason for inclusion as either 'UnitsStats' or 'EnrollmentStats'. The columns should be: school name, department name, average total units, total units range, total units variance, total enrollment, most popular course, course enrollment, and reason. Do not return any rounded answers."
