ative subject-offering fact tables / catalogs / directories. Per `concept_subject_offering_facts` decision guide, COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED is the only table carrying catalog attributes + ACADEMIC_YEAR + TOTAL_UNITS together; per `column_concept_enrollment_measures`, TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS is the textbook-program enrollment headcount used in the precedent Engineering-enrollment metrics.\n\n**Metrics**: dw_2151 (2022 degree-granting dept unit avg/variance — same filter shape), dw_4387 & dw_3868 (Engineering dept total enrollment > 50 via SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ STUDENT_DEPARTMENT — identical join triple), dw_1350 (dept/school stats with per-school rollup rows — same rollup shape), dw_3268 (union of two result sets with a \"Reason\" column — same output shape), dw_3237/dw_4650 (Engineering enrollment context).\n\n**Concepts**: concept_subject_offering_facts, concept_department_dimension, concept_course_catalog_sources, concept_course_material_programs, concept_academic_term_dimension — all retrieved; they document granularity/enrollment-semantics differences and the SIS_DEPARTMENT vs STUDENT_DEPARTMENT attribute split (SIS_DEPARTMENT carries SCHOOL_NAME + IS_DEGREE_GRANTING; STUDENT_DEPARTMENT does not).\n\n**Column concepts**: column_concept_total_units (decision guide: catalog unit statistics → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS), column_concept_department_name (DEPARTMENT_NAME vs OFFER_DEPT_NAME conventions; code joins preferred), column_concept_enrollment_measures (TIP NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS for textbook-program scope), column_concept_subject_id, column_concept_term_code, column_concept_year_columns (ACADEMIC_YEAR is the correct year system for \"2022 academic year\").\n\n## 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Join keys confirmed by column definitions: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE.COURSE_NUMBER ↔ SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE; SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.COURSE ↔ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_CODE; SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE; STUDENT_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_CODE ↔ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.OFFER_DEPT_CODE.\n- Precedent lineage: dw_4387/dw_3868 SQL literally contains the triple join `SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ STUDENT_DEPARTMENT` with `SCHOOL_NAME='Engineering'` and `HAVING SUM(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) > 50`. dw_1350 demonstrates the per-school rollup-row pattern (department name NULL). dw_3268 demonstrates the UNION ALL + Reason-column pattern.\n\n## 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix (evidence-cited):**\n\n| Dimension | COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED | SUBJECT_SUMMARY / SUBJECT_OFFERED_SUMMARY | TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | subject offering per term/academic year (catalog) | subject/cluster per term (registrar) | subject per term, textbook-program scope |\n| TOTAL_UNITS | yes (column_concept_total_units) | yes | **no** (concept_subject_offering_facts: \"Unit measures: None\") |\n| Enrollment | **none** | SUBJECT_ENROLLMENT_NUMBER etc. | NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS |\n| ACADEMIC_YEAR column | yes | via term join | via term join |\n\n| Dimension | SIS_DEPARTMENT | STUDENT_DEPARTMENT |\n|---|---|---|\n| SCHOOL_NAME | yes | yes |\n| IS_DEGREE_GRANTING | yes | **no** (concept_department_dimension comparison) |\n| Role in precedents | filter source | join companion in dw_4387/dw_3868 |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness:**\n- \"average/range/variance of total units, 2022 academic year, degree-granting\" → COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED.TOTAL_UNITS + ACADEMIC_YEAR: SUPPORTED; SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.IS_DEGREE_GRANTING/DEPARTMENT/DEPARTMENT_NAME/SCHOOL_NAME: SUPPORTED; SIS_SUBJECT_CODE join: SUPPORTED (gold mapping). TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED: NOT-SUPPORTED (no TOTAL_UNITS). SUBJECT_SUMMARY: SUPPORTED for units but VIOLATES the gold mapping/precedent (dw_2151 uses COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED for the identical 2022 shape).\n- \"total student enrollment > 50, School of Engineering, degree-granting, exclude Course 15, most popular course\" → SIS_DEPARTMENT (SCHOOL_NAME, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING, DEPARTMENT_CODE): SUPPORTED; TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED (NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS, SUBJECT_TITLE): SUPPORTED; STUDENT_DEPARTMENT: SUPPORTED as precedent join companion (1:1 on DEPARTMENT_CODE, no fan-out).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring:** \"school name\" → SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.SCHOOL_NAME (part 1) per gold mapping; \"department name\" → SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION.DEPARTMENT_NAME (part 1) / SIS_DEPARTMENT.DEPARTMENT_NAME (part 2); \"Mathematics (Course 18)\" → `DEPARTMENT_NAME <> 'Mathematics' AND DEPARTMENT <> '18'` (domain knowledge); \"Management (Course 15)\" → `DEPARTMENT_CODE <> '15'`; \"degree-granting\" → `IS_DEGREE_GRANTING = 'Y'`; \"most popular course\" → TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED.SUBJECT_TITLE at MAX(NUM_ENROLLED_STUDENTS) per department; \"reason\" → literal 'UnitsStats'/'EnrollmentStats' (dw_3268 precedent).\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence:** 2022-degree-granting unit-stats precedents on COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED: dw_2151, dw_104, dw_1049 (3). Engineering enrollment > 50 precedents on SIS_DEPARTMENT⋈TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED⋈STUDENT_DEPARTMENT: dw_4387, dw_3868 (2). School-rollup precedent: dw_1350 (1). Reason-column UNION precedent: dw_3268 (1).\n\n## 4. Business Usage\nCOURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED serves catalog unit-statistics questions (avg/variance/range of TOTAL_UNITS by department/year). SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION + SIS_SUBJECT_CODE serve degree-granting/course-level attribution. SIS_DEPARTMENT + TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED + STUDENT_DEPARTMENT serve per-department enrollment totals and most-popular-course questions in the textbook-program scope.\n\n## 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated: 6 gold tables via semantic_get (full columns); 8 related tables screened via concept_subject_offering_facts / concept_department_dimension / column_concept comparisons; 7 metrics via semantic_get (dw_2151, dw_4387, dw_1350, dw_3268, dw_3868 full SQL; dw_3237, dw_4650 via search desc); 5 concepts and 6 column concepts via semantic_get/search desc. mysql_query attempted 4 times — all failed with access-denied (noted explicitly; verification by execution impossible).\n\n## 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Part 1: SIS_SUBJECT_CODE ⋈ SIS_COURSE_DESCRIPTION ⋈ COURSE_CATALOG_SUBJECT_OFFERED, filters ACADEMIC_YEAR=2022, IS_DEGREE_GRANTING='Y', exclude Mathematics/18, GROUP BY SCHOOL_NAME, DEPARTMENT_NAME WITH ROLLUP, HAVING SCHOOL_NAME IS NOT NULL (per-school grand total with NULL dept name). Part 2: SIS_DEPARTMENT ⋈ TIP_SUBJECT_OFFERED ⋈ STUDENT_DEPARTMENT, Engineering + degree-granting + dept ≠ '15', HAVING SUM > 50, most popular course via correlated MAX subquery. UNION ALL with Reason literals.\n\n**6b.** Single WITH clause holding both branches; 9 output columns in asked order; NULLs for non-applicable columns per branch (dw_3268 pattern). STUDENT_DEPARTMENT is 1:1 per DEPARTMENT_CODE → no fan-out. VARIANCE() used unrounded per \"do not return rounded answers\".\n\n**6c.** Data: TOTAL_UNITS exists only in catalog table among candidates; TIP enrollment is the precedent measure. Semantic-network: decision guides of column_concept_total_units, column_concept_enrollment_measures, concept_department_dimension all point to these choices. Business: dw_2151/dw_4387/dw_3868/dw_1350/dw_3268 are exact-shape precedents.\n\n**6d.** No tie: gold mapping + precedents converge uniquely.\n\n",
